= August Thalheimer

The party's theorist since Luxemburg's death, a scholar from Württemberg with thick glasses. Brandler's closest ally, he argues that communists must win the masses with concrete demands they can fight for today.

- @programme
- @transitional
- @root: Return to main

@programme
title: Draft a Programme
subtitle: Long articles in the theoretical journal. The party's thinking moves to the Right.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if advisor_action_timer = 1 : Next advisor action in 1 month. ?][? if advisor_action_timer > 1 : Next advisor action in [+ advisor_action_timer +] months. ?]
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.advisor_action_timer = 4;
Q.last_advisor_action = 1;
Q.lean_unionist += 3;
Q.unity += 3;
!}

Thalheimer answers every critic in print, at length, with footnotes. Fewer comrades read him than should, but those who do start to argue his way.

@transitional
title: Transitional Demands
subtitle: Workers' control and a tax on real values. The Left calls it reformism.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if advisor_action_timer = 1 : Next advisor action in 1 month. ?][? if advisor_action_timer > 1 : Next advisor action in [+ advisor_action_timer +] months. ?]
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.advisor_action_timer = 4;
Q.last_advisor_action = 1;
Q.worker_support += 5;
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 5;
!}

Thalheimer writes that the party needs demands the workers can fight for this year: control of the factories, taxes on the propertied, bread for the unemployed. The factory papers reprint the list.
